    "flags": {
        "cinderfall": {
            "tagline": "Everyone else in the soul economy binds a ghost to a machine and calls it labor. You bind one to yourself, sit down across from it, and negotiate like it still gets a vote — because it does, and it remembers every time you forgot that.",
            "role": "Negotiator with the Dead — slow trust, sharp debts",
            "pillar": "Spirit / Faith",
            "hpFormula": "8 + Con / level",
            "keyAbilityText": "Wisdom",
            "spellcastingText": "Occult, prepared (Wisdom)",
            "spellcastingTradition": "occult",
            "spellcastingPreparation": "prepared",
            "terms": [
                [
                    "The Hollow",
                    "Your bound vessel — a corroded saint's mask, a reliquary box wired crooked into your sternum, a conductor's lantern with no bulb left in it. Whatever shape it takes, it's the one thing every wandering soul you've ever struck a deal with has had to move through. Lose it and you lose everything downstream of it."
                ],
                [
                    "Quiet / Unveiled",
                    "Your two working states. Quiet is the spirit sitting latent behind the Hollow's seal — you get its patience, its trade-knowledge, its quiet utility. Unveiled is you letting it rise all the way to the surface for a scene — sharper, stronger, and no longer entirely you."
                ],
                [
                    "The Toll",
                    "What you owe. Every favor asked of the spirit adds weight to the Toll; every night's rest and honest conversation pays some of it back down. Let it run high enough, or spend past what's fair in a single ask, and the spirit stops being generous about how it collects."
                ],
                [
                    "Parley",
                    "The act of asking — your version of casting a spell. You don't recite words at the dead. You make a case, and the Hollow carries your case to whoever's currently housed inside it. Mechanically this is prepared occult spellcasting: each day you prepare cantrips and spells from the occult list (in <em>What You Learned</em>) and cast them using Wisdom against your Parley DC. Vessel spells and pushing an ask for extra Toll build on top of that base."
                ],
                [
                    "Fraying",
                    "What happens when a Parley asks for more than the spirit is willing to give and the Toll can't cover the difference. Never fatal on its own. Never pleasant either."
                ],
                [
                    "Drifters",
                    "The setting's word, borrowed by every Hollowbound alive, for the ordinary unhoused dead still wandering the wastes — the raw population you might, with time and risk, talk into the Hollow once your current arrangement runs its course."
                ]
            ],
